      "parentFingerprint": "1100aaa1bd744ed497133813e0af276d8bbe1cfe2736c57d182b83a73aa79577",
      "passageSha256": "7d986056672f5d41a4fa50ccb0c4e44f1f34fe269b5344b6c2b571983e5cd905",
      "pdfPages": [
        73
      ]
    },
    {
      "order": 10,
      "questionId": "qe-c07-0067",
      "sentenceId": "c07-s03-p073-03210-s002",
      "sentenceText": "Swiss psychologist René Proyer has studied adult playfulness more intensely than anyone I know.",
      "sentenceSha256": "f779e9874997209ecc5ee0f7b9f36497b4df82ad722d814b35c69473a794143b",
      "readingUnitId": "c07-s03-p073-03210-r001-004",
      "parentQuestionId": "q-c07-039",
      "parentFingerprint": "1100aaa1bd744ed497133813e0af276d8bbe1cfe2736c57d182b83a73aa79577",
      "passageSha256": "7d986056672f5d41a4fa50ccb0c4e44f1f34fe269b5344b6c2b571983e5cd905",
      "pdfPages": [
        73
      ]
    },
    {
      "order": 11,
      "questionId": "qe-c07-0068",
      "sentenceId": "c07-s03-p073-03210-s004",
      "sentenceText": "It is “an openness to being a fool, which is a combination of not worrying about competence, not being self-important, not taking norms as sacred and finding ambiguity and double edges a source of wisdom and delight.”",
      "sentenceSha256": "937d46ba5ccac40867e23b501c767e00d5eab80015a4551a89209d27febe6890",
      "readingUnitId": "c07-s03-p073-03210-r001-004",
      "parentQuestionId": "q-c07-039",
      "parentFingerprint": "1100aaa1bd744ed497133813e0af276d8bbe1cfe2736c57d182b83a73aa79577",
      "passageSha256": "7d986056672f5d41a4fa50ccb0c4e44f1f34fe269b5344b6c2b571983e5cd905",
      "pdfPages": [
        73
      ]
    },
    {
      "order": 12,
      "questionId": "qe-c07-0069",
      "sentenceId": "c07-s03-p073-04965-s001",
      "sentenceText": "In a 2013 paper, Proyer found that playful people are slightly more satisfied with their lives than those who are less playful.",
      "sentenceSha256": "5bbdc65d9da0047c0c3ff39c71c20678c6993e4e2f077ae2c8058815fabd7e38",
      "readingUnitId": "c07-s03-p073-04965-r001-004",
      "parentQuestionId": "q-c07-041",
      "parentFingerprint": "645467a1d7ca5891f870e28581b1df963f2188c57c50b7af730f52b33d693d41",
      "passageSha256": "1eea911088423fbd87c7e672870fbe4ca215a666b694a9a0def3d4bdd915a874",
      "pdfPages": [
        73
      ]
    },
    {
      "order": 13,
      "questionId": "qe-c07-0070",
      "sentenceId": "c07-s03-p073-04965-s002",
      "sentenceText": "He also discovered that happy people enjoyed communing with nature, whereas playful people did not.",
      "sentenceSha256": "fb1355903a1e8011e45474f2e41e27a0531017c3b955560230d675370c973e76",
      "readingUnitId": "c07-s03-p073-04965-r001-004",
      "parentQuestionId": "q-c07-041",
      "parentFingerprint": "645467a1d7ca5891f870e28581b1df963f2188c57c50b7af730f52b33d693d41",
      "passageSha256": "1eea911088423fbd87c7e672870fbe4ca215a666b694a9a0def3d4bdd915a874",
      "pdfPages": [
        73
      ]
    },
    {
      "order": 14,
      "questionId": "qe-c07-0071",
      "sentenceId": "c07-s03-p073-04965-s003",
      "sentenceText": "In contrast, happy people did not particularly enjoy going on vacation, whereas playful people did.",
      "sentenceSha256": "f1e2da6d53dcf400018b8f94c4749bd3f3d1af53482b127fa3af4ec2639be94d",
      "readingUnitId": "c07-s03-p073-04965-r001-004",
